{"run": "exp-017-bucket-audit-tiny", "type": "report", "a": {"bundle": "artifacts/agent", "abstraction": "tiny", "generate_deals": 60}, "delta_mb": null, "ci": null, "sprt": null, "promote": false, "seatings": 294, "notes": "EXP-017 bucket-quality audit on the tiny abstraction. Realized-EV-per-bucket from 60 deals/opponent, flop+turn hero decisions. between=6997544.1649 within=29401041.9619 ratio=0.2380 (n=294). Ratio < 1 means the current buckets do NOT separate realized-EV differences well — within-bucket variance dominates. This is the signal the EMD-rebuild (§4.1 / v3 A2) is meant to move: a better partition of the same space should raise between/within. Recorded as a baseline for the future EMD comparison; NO EMD rebuild run yet.", "ts": 1790449547}
{"run": "exp-019-preflop-equity-cold-warm", "type": "bench", "a": {"bench": "cham-eval/benches/preflop_equity.rs", "metric": "cold vs warm preflop_equity"}, "delta_mb": null, "ci": null, "sprt": null, "promote": false, "seatings": 0, "notes": "EXP-019 keep/kill decision data. Cold=254.57ms [234.97, 274.32] per call (full 1.7M-combo equity_exact vs a singleton villain range on empty board). Warm=16.052ns [15.813, 16.398] per call (hashmap hit). Ratio ~1.6e7x. VERDICT: memoization alone is sufficient when preflop all-in spots recur (which they do — the same (hero,villain) combo pair hits the same key). An offline GPU table is only justified if cold paths fire on sufficiently many DISTINCT combos that the 254ms-per-cold cost dominates a session. Given 1.7M possible pairs and typical session lengths, cold-dominated workloads are implausible: KEEP the memoized CPU implementation, CLOSE EXP-019 as 'memoization sufficient, GPU table NOT warranted'.", "ts": 1790450149}
{"run": "exp-017-emd-exact-build", "type": "report", "a": {"profile": "exact", "config": "config/abstraction-tiny.toml", "out": "artifacts/buckets-exact"}, "delta_mb": null, "ci": null, "sprt": null, "promote": false, "seatings": 0, "notes": "v3 §4.1 A2 CPU validation scale. BuildParams::exact (2000 flop orbits + 2000 turn orbits, exhaustive next-street equity histograms) feeds kmeans_l1 (EMD = L1 on CDFs) at the SAME k as tiny (flop k=32, turn k=16). Meta confirms feature=nextstreet_cdf16_exact runs=0 vs tiny feature=river_cdf16 runs=8 — the EMD-style feature is now proven at CPU scale (runs end-to-end, writes flop.bin/turn.bin/meta.json in ~1 min). Partition bytes differ from tiny (see commit). HONEST NEXT STEP: comparing exact-vs-tiny quality needs a RETRAIN of the 5 blueprints (robust + 4 experts) against the new bucket dir — abstraction_hash changes, so the existing tiny-trained policies will not load. Then re-run audit-buckets --generate + exploitability on both bundles. That retrain is the multi-hour GPU-scale job the roadmap defers to §4.2 job 1; this entry records only the CPU validation scale as DONE.", "ts": 1790452493}
